+# A hand-rolled structure, and the three obligations of `unsafe`
+
+Every step before this one denied `unsafe` — `unsafe_code = "deny"` stood in the manifest from `5.1`,
+and none of them needed it. This step needs it for one structure, and the point of the step is that a
+structure which needs it can **argue** for it: three obligations, each one named, each one checked.
+
+## The structure
+
+A bounded, single-producer single-consumer ring of `MaybeUninit<T>`. It exists because a queue's whole
+job is to avoid the cost of a lock on the path between two threads, and a safe version either locks or
+allocates per message. The ring does neither: two atomics and a slot array.
+
+## The three obligations
+
+1. **Initialisation.** A slot is uninitialised until a `push` writes it. Reading a slot nobody wrote is
+   the bug `MaybeUninit` exists to prevent, and the queue's invariant is what makes every read sound:
+   the producer writes at `tail % capacity`, the consumer reads at `head % capacity`, and
+   `head <= tail` says the slot was written before it is read.
+2. **Exclusive access.** The producer's write and the consumer's read touch different slots *by the
+   index arithmetic*, and the indices are atomics with the right orderings: `Release` when an index is
+   published, `Acquire` when it is observed. That ordering pair is the entire synchronisation — there
+   is no lock, which is the point, and there is no fence, which is luck: the pair is what the argument
+   uses.
+3. **Drop exactly once.** A value in the ring when it is dropped has to be dropped once: the `Drop`
+   impl drops the slots between `head` and `tail`, and nothing else. Dropping twice is worse than
+   leaking, and dropping nothing is a leak nobody sees until the queue is busy.
+
+Each block carries a `// SAFETY:` note saying which obligation it rests on — the gate
+(`unsafe-budget@5`) counts the blocks and requires the notes, which is why the number in the metadata
+is the number of blocks here.
+
+## What checks it
+
+- **`loom`** runs every interleaving of the index protocol, in two models: a value published with
+  `Release` is seen once with `Acquire`, and a slot is not reused before the consumer has moved `head`
+  past it. That is the part of the argument a test can hold.
+- **`miri` is not available** on this course's pinned toolchain (`1.98.1-aarch64` has no `miri`
+  component — handoff M4 §1). The step says so rather than pretending: loom plus the written argument
+  is the evidence it has, and the page names what is missing.
+
+## What the gate counts
+
+`unsafe-budget@5` allows five occurrences of the word `unsafe` in production code, requires a
+`// SAFETY:` note within three lines above each, and — because the budget is no longer zero — does not
+require the manifest to deny `unsafe_code`. The step's own manifest drops the deny, and the comment
+where it stood says which step argued for that and why.
